;; forms lens (PLAN-005, PLAN-011 W6) — turns whose PROGRAM calls a given tool
;; OR runs a given shell command head.
;;
;; Mirrors SpellAgent.Hist.Query.forms: returns the nodes (seq-ordered, as
;; projected maps) whose form AST contains either a (tool/<name> ...) call
;; (when data/tool is set) or a shell command with the given head run via
;; (tool/sh {:argv [head ...]}) / (tool/sh-pipe {:stages ...}) (when data/shell
;; is set). Pure transform over the injected `data/nodes` projection.
;;
;; Each node carries two pre-extracted lists (Elixir cannot pass the raw AST
;; into the sandbox, so the names are surfaced):
;;   "form_tools"  — Lisp tool-call names in the AST    (matched by data/tool)
;;   "form_shells" — shell command heads in the AST      (matched by data/shell)
;; Dispatch order (shell first) and the blank-guard MUST mirror
;; SpellAgent.Hist.Namespace.forms/3 exactly so the PTC lens and the Elixir
;; fast path return identical nodes for identical args (the parity contract).
(->> data/nodes
     (filter (fn [n]
               (if (and data/shell (not= data/shell ""))
                 (contains? (get n "form_shells") data/shell)
                 (contains? (get n "form_tools") data/tool)))))
